00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:13.390
next year and tonight I’ll be doing a breakdown
of the Marvel Special.

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:17.230
They’ll be some new footage from the set
of Avengers 2.

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:18.770
If you’re finding me for the first time,
be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:23.520
I’ve bookmarked Tuesdays as Marvel days
just because I’m already doing videos for

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:24.520
SHIELD.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:31.289
If there’s any movie you want me to do a
video for just write your suggestion in the

00:00:31.289 --> 00:00:32.289
comments.

00:00:32.289 --> 00:00:38.219
So here’s 5 major things you need to know
about Ant-Man

00:00:38.219 --> 00:00:40.159
Number 5 - Elephant In The Room.

00:00:40.159 --> 00:00:44.969
There’s one tiny, super major detail they
changed about the characters.

00:00:44.969 --> 00:00:50.850
In the comics Hank Pym the first Ant-Man creates
Ultron, the Avengers most infamous villain.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:54.719
But because of the way Marvel’s movies have
unfolded and because they want all the stories

00:00:54.719 --> 00:00:56.889
to integrate, they had to change that.

00:00:56.889 --> 00:01:02.619
I covered Ultron’s new origin in the Avengers
2 video I did last week, but the Ant-Man movie

00:01:02.619 --> 00:01:07.350
if it does feature Ultron, will focus mostly
on a different Ant-Man, the Scott Lang version

00:01:07.350 --> 00:01:08.350
of the character.

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:13.530
Quick side note, regardless of the plot of
Avengers 2, I am so hoping there’s an Ultron

00:01:13.530 --> 00:01:14.530
cameo in Ant-Man.

00:01:14.530 --> 00:01:17.330
It would be blasphemous if there weren’t.

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:23.580
Number 4 - The movie will feature Hank Pym,
played by Michael Douglas, but the main character

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:26.430
is really Scott Lang, the second Ant-Man.

00:01:26.430 --> 00:01:31.780
If you’re not familiar with the comics,
Scott Lang’s run as the character was less

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:35.520
of a dark angsty story and more of a fun series
of adventures.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:40.470
Hank Pym was like a version of Tony Stark,
genius inventor who develops the Ant-Man suit.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:44.750
Scott Lang was actually a criminal who stole
the Ant-Man suit to save his daughter.

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:49.491
Over time Hank Pym then kind of became an
Obi-Wan Kenobi to him and helped him become

00:01:49.491 --> 00:01:50.491
a real hero.

00:01:50.491 --> 00:01:55.010
It will also star Michael Pena and Patrick
Wilson.

00:01:55.010 --> 00:01:59.170
We don’t know who there charcters will be
and we don’t know if The Wasp, Janet Van

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:01.390
Dyne’s character will be featured.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:05.830
But I would at least expect her to be referenced.

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:11.310
Rashida Jones is rumored to be in talks, so
she would be a good candidate for The Wasp.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:18.330
There is a third version of Ant-Man in the
comics, Eric O’Grady, but he probably won’t

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:19.500
be part of the story.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:24.400
It’s really just going to be Paul Rudd and
super hero jedi master Michael Douglas.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:30.040
Number 3 - The movie is the beginning of Phase
3, coming just 3 months after Avengers 2.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:35.370
So they will probably address some of the
things that happen during that movie.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:40.440
The Avengers will probably defeat but not
kill Ultron and the infinity gems storyline

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:41.870
will develop more.

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:47.510
Plus there’s the continuing Presence of
Coulson and SHIELD.

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:53.730
I’d say Nick Fury too, but all of the teasers
for Captain America make it seem like he dies.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:57.439
I think it would be foolish to assume that
he will, if they brought Coulson back from

00:02:57.439 --> 00:02:58.439
the dead.

00:02:58.439 --> 00:02:59.950
They can bring Fury back too.

00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:04.249
That being said Phase 3 will be the era of
‘quote unqote’ miracles.

00:03:04.249 --> 00:03:08.409
Meaning mutant abilities and more fantastical
stories.

00:03:08.409 --> 00:03:09.409
Like Magic.

00:03:09.409 --> 00:03:15.010
It will also feature a changing Avengers roster.

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:19.169
Different types of villains, like Ultron and
Thanos, require different types of super heroes.

00:03:19.169 --> 00:03:23.090
Number 2 - The movie is directed by Edgar
Wright of Cornetto Trilogy Fame.

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:26.269
If you haven’t seen any of his other movies,
get on it.

00:03:26.269 --> 00:03:27.269
They’re all amazing.

00:03:27.269 --> 00:03:30.779
He’s mostly famous for Shaun of the Dead,
Hot Fuzz and now World’s End.

00:03:30.779 --> 00:03:33.569
But he’s also done a ton of other awesome
stuff.

00:03:33.569 --> 00:03:37.470
And on top of that, he has a blog that he
posts awesome stuff to on a regular basis.

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:43.730
One of the things I love about Marvel directors
like Edgar Wright and James Gunn who did Guardians,

00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:45.669
is that they’re highly engaged with the
fandom.

00:03:45.669 --> 00:03:50.919
It’s like when I do Q&amp;A videos and include
your comments or do videos based on your suggestions.

00:03:50.919 --> 00:03:55.260
It’s just makes things so much more fun
when you know the creative person behind all

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:58.069
this is listening to you and cares about what
you think.

00:03:58.069 --> 00:04:01.099
and number 1 - Remember how I just said the
Avengers roster will be changing.

00:04:01.099 --> 00:04:05.959
Well in the comics, under the tutelage of
Obi-Wan Hank Pym, Scott Lang becomes part

00:04:05.959 --> 00:04:07.090
of the Avengers.

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:08.090
You can see where this is going.

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:12.269
It’s going to be like the first Iron Man
movie, when Nick Fury and Coulson approached

00:04:12.269 --> 00:04:13.569
Tony Stark.

00:04:13.569 --> 00:04:19.050
Avengers 3 is a long way off, but it’s likely
then that Paul Rudd will be one of the second

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:21.690
tier Avengers in that movie, like Black Widow
and Hawkeye.

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:25.780
We don’t know what parts of the comics they’re
including in the story, but if you want to

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:30.440
read the comics with Scott Lang’s run as
Ant-Man start with Avengers number 181.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:35.550
He didn’t become Ant-Man until Marvel Premiere
number 47.

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:39.510
But both those are from 1979, so this was
a long time ago.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:42.780
The cool thing that Marvel does though is
discount the comics associated with movies

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:43.780
that are coming up.

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:47.660
So like right now, there’s a big discount
on Comixology for Captain America comic books.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:56.720
Quick Bonus point - A big part of Scott Lang’s
run as the character was Pym Particles, because

00:04:56.720 --> 00:05:03.090
Star Wars ran afoul of midichlorians I think
Marvel might side-step the issue.

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:06.960
But a core part of Hank Pym’s character
is that he’s mentally unstable as a result

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:08.880
of repeated exposure to Pym Particles.

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:13.720
I’ll be interested to see how Michael Douglas
portrays this on screen.

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:20.050
I always thought of Pym as a crazier version
of Tony Stark.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:23.900
Which kind of explains how he could create
Ultron.

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:28.130
But since the movies are changing all that,
they might change Pym’s personality a little

00:05:28.130 --> 00:05:31.580
too.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:36.820
So now it’s your turn, what are you hoping
to see in Ant-Man and do you think they’ll

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:39.510
have any Ultron easter eggs?

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:43.360
Marvel has become famous for easter eggs and
post credits scenes.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:47.880
Remember the next movie after Ant-Man is Captain
America 3.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:51.310
So SHIELD is definitely going to be featured
at the end of this movie.

